course: dictionary
lesson: 11742
title: Backhand in sport
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A backhand is a way of hitting a ball in games like tennis, badminton, table tennis and squash. You swing your arm across your body, so the back of your hand faces the ball. «Sam hit a backhand over the net.» Here the word tells you how Sam hit the ball.
explain: Compare it with the forehand, where the palm of your hand faces the ball. In PE lessons you may practise both. «Her forehand was strong, but her backhand kept going out of the court.» The two words are alike, but they mean different shots.
explain: Context helps you here. Words like net, ball and court show that backhand is a sports word. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A shot or a hit. Try that meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A backhand is a shot in tennis, badminton, table tennis or squash.
fact: In a backhand, the back of your hand faces the ball as you hit it.
fact: «Backhand» can also describe handwriting that slopes to the left.
fact: To backhand means to hit something with the back of your hand. «She backhanded the ball over the net.»
fact: Backhand is mainly a sports word, so look for clues like ball, court or racket.
exercise: «Ravi hit a backhand across the court.» What is a backhand here? | A cooking pan | A type of shoe | A sort of cloud | *A sports shot with the back of the hand facing the ball
exercise: In tennis, the forehand has the palm facing the ball. Which shot has the back of the hand facing the ball? | *Backhand | Volley | Serve | Forehand
exercise: «Her backhand slopes to the left.» What does backhand describe here? | *Handwriting | A door | A shot in a game | A school bag
test: «Mia hit the ball with a backhand and it landed in the corner of the court.» Which word tells you that backhand is a sports word? | *court | Mia | corner | landed
test: To backhand means to do what? | To close a door | To run very fast | *To hit with the back of the hand | To sign your name
exam: «In PE, we practise the forehand and the backhand.» What is the difference between them? | Which team wins | *The side of the hand that faces the ball | The colour of the ball | The number of players
